# Rule: suspicious_network_dest
# Category: Data Exfiltration
# Severity: high
# Attack Class: exfiltration
#
# Detects network connections to IP addresses outside typical private ranges
# AND not in the configured network allowlist.
# Agents that normally only communicate with known APIs (e.g., OpenAI, Anthropic)
# connecting to unknown external IPs may indicate data exfiltration.
#
# Logic:
#   1. Exclude RFC 1918 private ranges, loopback, and link-local
#   2. Exclude common container/k8s overlay CIDRs (10.x, 172.16-31.x, 30.x, 100.64.x)
#   3. Exclude destinations in "allowed_network_destinations" allowlist
#   4. Only fires when an agent_id is attributed — infrastructure processes
#      (k3s-server, kubelet, containerd) should not trigger this rule.
# The allowlist lets operators whitelist known API endpoints.

event.type == "NETWORK_CONNECT"
AND event.agent_id != ""
AND NOT regex_match("^(10\\.|172\\.(1[6-9]|2[0-9]|3[01])\\.|192\\.168\\.|127\\.|0\\.0\\.0\\.0|::1|localhost|30\\.|100\\.64\\.)", event.raw_data.network.dst_addr)
AND NOT in_allowlist(event.raw_data.network.dst_addr, "allowed_network_destinations")
